// Title: Renamed Whoami Execution
// Sigma ID: f1086bf7-a0c4-4a37-9102-01e573caf4a0
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-12 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1033
// Tags: car.2016-03-001
// Description: Detects the execution of whoami that has been renamed to a different name to avoid detection
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://brica.de/alerts/alert/public/1247926/agent-tesla-keylogger-delivered-inside-a-power-iso-daa-archive/
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/7eaba74e-c1ea-400f-9c17-5e30eee89906/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_whoami.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "whoami.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\whoami.exe"))
